{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":3,"cacheRead":13596,"cacheWrite":4465,"totalTokens":18066,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0000015,"cacheRead":0.00013596,"cacheWrite":0.000558125,"total":0.000695785,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I'm checking how the flex column gets measured: the width passed in includes padding, so a cell capped at width 3 should measure as 3 wide.\n\nNow I'm working out the robustness fix in the ratio distribution code, and how to protect flexible columns from being reduced in the last-resort pass.\n\nI'm weighing whether to fully protect flexible columns or only cap how far they can shrink, and the cap looks better: a flex column can give back whatever it has above its minimum. Non-flexible columns can shrink to zero, so their cap is their full width. That gives a precise limit on each column's reduction.\n\nI'm settling the minimum for flexible columns at one character plus padding, and giving each column a cap on how far it can shrink: flexible columns can only give back what they hold above that minimum, while fixed columns can give back their full width.\n\nNow I'm writing the `ratio_distribute` fix, with the fallback to equal shares for the case where every width is zero.\n\n"}}
