{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking how the flex column gets measured: the width passed in includes padding, so a cell capped at width 3 should measure as 3 wide.\n\nNow I'm working out the robustness fix in the ratio distribution code, and how to protect flexible columns from being reduced in the last-resort pass.\n\nI'm weighing whether to fully protect flexible columns or only cap how far they can shrink, and the cap looks better: a flex column can give back whatever it has above its minimum. Non-flexible columns can shrink to zero, so their cap is their full width. That gives a precise limit on each column's reduction.\n\nI'm settling the minimum for flexible columns at one character plus padding, and giving each column a cap on how far it can shrink: flexible columns can only give back what they hold above that minimum, while fixed columns can give back their full width.\n\nNow I'm writing the `ratio_distribute` fix, with the fallback to equal shares for the case where every width is zero.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The fix has two parts:\n\n1. **Last-resort collapse** (`table.py`): the even reduction should only shrink a flexible column down to its minimum of one content cell plus padding. Each column gets a shrink cap, so the flexible columns keep their minimum width.\n2. **`ratio_distribute`** (`_ratio.py`): it asserts on all-zero ratios and goes negative on negative totals. I'll make it fall back to equal shares, return `[]` for no slots, and clamp the total at zero."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_016KNKnr4HcYiq5tKjb3z6U4","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/app/rich/_ratio.py","oldText":"    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list of integers guaranteed to sum to total.\n    \"\"\"\n    if minimums:\n        ratios = [ratio if _min else 0 for ratio, _min in zip(ratios, min